From: Vorapol Rinsatitnon <vorapol.r@pm.me>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 17:01:22 +1300
Subject: [PATCH] syscall: hold a link to its type where the kernel follows it regardless

Windows 10 22H2 and 11 refuse a junction or directory symlink that leads
to a file, and a file symlink that leads to a directory. Windows 7, 8 and
8.1 open whatever is there, and some early versions of Windows 10 still
follow a junction to a file. The os.Root tests of a security fix
(CL 847305, commit b19851b, Go 1.28) expect the refusal.

Give the refusal on those systems too. There syscall.Open now refuses
such links.

	                       before                 after
	-----------------------------------------------------------------------
	Windows 7, 8, 8.1,     such a link opens      refused, as on 22H2
	some early Windows 10  what it leads to
	-----------------------------------------------------------------------
	Windows 10 22H2, 11    refused                refused

Gate: version, then query (Windows 10 before 22H2) | Remembered: Y

